\title{Blocking spin fields}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{For the scalar-field refinement in \ref{fdip-01BW}, the index comparison of \ref{fdip-01BZ} uses flux and the free bulk integer. The exact calculation in \ref{fdip-01BQ} rules out pointwise restriction as an intertwiner of the centered operators. Can a different map of spin fields intertwine the Wilson kernels on a specified pair of grids and scalar connections?}
